cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this code, cite Godot Engine, whose API it re-implements.
title: godot-lite, a namespaced Godot API shim for sandbox guests
abstract: >-
  A hand-written stand-in for the parts of Godot's core that Cassie's
  curvenet subset (vendor/cassie) and the vendored Godot core subset
  (vendor/godot-core-subset) include, at Godot's include paths and in
  namespace gdl, so the Cassie sources compile almost verbatim with no
  engine: memory.h (memnew/memdelete over malloc), error_macros.h (the
  ERR_*/WARN_*/CRASH_* macros in use), a String over std::string, a
  copy-on-write Vector over a shared std::vector, Variant with the types
  Cassie moves (bool, int, float, String, Vector3, Object, Callable,
  Dictionary, Array, PackedInt32/Float32/Vector3Array), Array and
  Dictionary as shared references (the Dictionary on Godot's own
  insertion-ordered HashMap), TypedArray, Callable over std::function with
  callable_mp, Object/RefCounted/Ref, no-op ClassDB and GDCLASS, a
  synchronous WorkerThreadPool, Resource, Node3D, Mesh/ArrayMesh, OS
  environment and Time ticks. gdl_prelude.h (force-included into Cassie
  TUs) is `using namespace gdl`. Mostly new code; these parts follow
  Godot's source at the pin closely enough to cite it: Ref<T> and the
  RefCounted reference protocol (core/object/ref_counted.h), the
  memory.h templates and the _GlobalNil sentinel (core/os/memory.h), the
  Vector method set including sort_custom/slice/bsearch
  (core/templates/vector.h), the Variant type enum numbering, the
  Mesh::ArrayType values and Dictionary::next (core/variant/dictionary.cpp).
  tests/native/godot_lite checks it natively against Godot's own Curve3D
  unit-test expectations and a Godot 4.7.2 run.
type: software
authors:
  - name: V-Sekai-fire
  - name: Godot Engine contributors
    website: https://godotengine.org
